.TH fold 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
fold \- wrap each input line to fit in specified width
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY fold
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Wrap input lines in each FILE, writing to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fold\-b
\fB\-b, \-\-bytes\fP
.UE
count bytes rather than columns
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fold\-c
\fB\-c, \-\-characters\fP
.UE
count characters rather than columns
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fold\-s
\fB\-s, \-\-spaces\fP
.UE
break after blanks, or in words greater than WIDTH
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fold\-w
\fB\-w, \-\-width=\,WIDTH\fP
.UE
use WIDTH columns instead of 80
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/fold#fold\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/fold#fold\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
